            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0779" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v11/pg750"/>

                <head>273. Memorandum From the Presidentʼs Deputy Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Haig) to the
                    Presidentʼs Assistant for National Security Affairs (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d273-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1971-12-10">December 10, 1971</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    Henry:</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">name not declassified</hi>] called and said that the
                    Jordanians have replied as follows. They will send four aircraft with Jordanian
                    pilots immediately to Pakistan. The Paks asked for 12, but he will hold to four
                    initially to see how it goes. He is prepared to go as high as 22 ultimately.</p>
                <p>Attached is a message from Raza<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d273-f2"/> referring to six F–5ʼs which the Turks have
                    apparently agreed to provide if the U.S.
                    agrees.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">AH</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d273-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d273-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon
                    Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 643,
                    Country Files, Middle East, India/Pakistan, December 1–10. Top Secret;
                    Sensitive.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d273-f2" n="2" xml:id="d273-f2-content">
                <p>Attached but not printed is a December 9 letter to Kissinger from Ambassador Raza.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
